%T A398634 6,12,28,90,5040,1,1,2,6,24,48,152,646,40320,1,1,2,6,24,72,240,952,
%U A398634 5242,362880,1,1,2,6,24,120,336,1392,7208,47622,3628800
%N A398634 Square array A(n,k), n >= 0, k >= 0, read by antidiagonals downwards, where A(n,k) is the number of permutations p of [n] such that |p(i+1)-p(i)| <>  k for all 1 <= i < n.
%H A398634 George Spahn and Doron Zeilberger, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.02550">Counting Permutations Where The Difference Between Entries Located r Places Apart Can never be s (For any given positive integers r and s)</a>, arXiv:2211.02550 [math.CO], 2022.
%F A398634 A(n,0) = n!.
%F A398634 A(n,k) = n! for n <= k.
%F A398634 A(n,k) = Sum_{j=0..n-k} (-2)^j * binomial(n-k,j) * (n-j)! for k < n <= 2*k.
%e A398634 Square array begins:
%e A398634         1,      1,      1,      1,      1,       1, ...
%e A398634         1,      1,      1,      1,      1,       1, ...
